<title>HONG KONG: HK dlr May M-3 rises 23.8 pct on year.</title>
<headline>HK dlr May M-3 rises 23.8 pct on year.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong Monetary Authority gave the following money supply figures as percentage changes:</p>
<p>				   May '97    April '97    May '96</p>
<p> HK dollar M-3 (year-on-year)  +23.8	+21.8	 +13.0</p>
<p> HK dollar M-3 (month)	    +1.6	 +3.2	  -0.1</p>
<p> HK dollar M-1 (year-on-year) +18.4	  +17.0	  +4.5</p>
<p> HK dollar M-1 (month)	   -0.3	   +3.8	  -1.4</p>
<p> HK dollar M-2 (year-on-year) +24.0	  +21.9	 +13.3</p>
<p> HK dollar M-2 (month)	   +1.6	   +3.3	  -0.1</p>
<p>Loans to finance visible trade of Hong Kong (year-on-year)</p>
<p>				    +4.1	   +2.5	  +8.9</p>
<p>Other loans for use in Hong Kong (year-on-year)</p>
<p>				   +25.8	  +25.0	 +13.0</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
